Remote-tracking ref churn is now a `repo.integrity_warning` on the run instead of a failed run — and the gate's last red stage (`make check-split`, live transcript fan-out to a passive web process) is fixed and green.

- `src/server/integrity.ts`: `checkRepoIntegrity` keeps its signature/return type and its `refWritesSince` / `waitForRepoLeaseRelease` logic, but classifies `refs/remotes/**` outside `ralph/` separately from hooks, `.git/config`, local branches and tags; `isManagedRef` still skips `refs/heads/ralph/*` and `refs/remotes/<remote>/ralph/*` entirely.
- `src/server/stage.ts`: the ref-only differences are emitted as a `repo.integrity_warning` event (payload `refs`, one entry per `ref moved` / `ref appeared` / `ref deleted`), so the run still completes; hooks/config/local-branch/tag differences still fail as before. `src/server/reviewService.ts` needed no change (`checkRefs: false`). No schema change.
- UI/docs: `src/app/card/[id]/page.tsx` renders the warning on the timeline; `docs/SANDBOXING.md`, `docs/TROUBLESHOOTING.md` and the spec-19 row of `docs/DESIGN_HISTORY.md` describe the new behaviour, and `specs/19-shared-git-ref-noise.md` carries an append-only dated amendment (nothing deleted).
- Gate repair, cause 1 — `src/server/transcript.ts`: a watcher is normally armed before the writer has created anything, so waiting for the file is event-driven: watch the deepest directory that exists, move that watch down as each level appears, catch up from cursor 0 the moment the file is there, with a 50 ms stat poll only as the backstop (it used to be the only mechanism, at 300 ms). A batch already being read when `stop()` lands is delivered instead of dropped.
- Gate repair, cause 2 — `src/server/transcriptWatchers.ts`: `syncRunWatcher` arms the watcher from the start *event*, not from the status the `runs` row happens to hold now, because the events tailer can hand it a whole finished run in one batch (`run.started` … `run.finished`); the same batch retires the watcher and the periodic scan reaps one whose finish never arrives. The scan still only watches rows in status `running`.
- Tests: `src/server/transcript.test.ts` (appear-by-directory-event, walk-down-to-a-new-run-directory, deliver-the-in-flight-batch) and `src/server/transcriptWatchers.test.ts` (whole run arriving in one batch after it settled). `make check-split` passed three consecutive runs; `lint`, `typecheck` and the transcript/scoping/stage/boot/eventsTail/integrity/reviewService unit files are green.